---
import "../styles/globals.css";
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://zentype.jonathanrreed.com";
const contactUrl = `${siteUrl}/contact/`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<SEO
			title="Zen Typer Feedback and Support"
			description="Contact Jonathan R. Reed about Zen Typer feedback, accessibility issues, typing practice improvements, privacy questions, or project details."
			canonical={contactUrl}
			keywords={[
				"Zen Typer contact",
				"typing practice feedback",
				"mindful typing support",
				"Jonathan R. Reed contact",
			]}
			breadcrumbItems={[
				{ name: "Mindful typing test", url: `${siteUrl}/` },
				{ name: "Contact Zen Typer", url: contactUrl },
			]}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main class="content-page px-6 pb-32 pt-16 text-text">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8">
				<nav aria-label="Primary" class="content-nav">
					<a href="/">Home</a>
					<a href="/quote/">Quote mode</a>
					<a href="/zen/">Zen mode</a>
					<a href="/about/">About</a>
					<a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
					<a href="/subprocessors/">Subprocessors</a>
				</nav>

				<article class="glass content-prose rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 space-y-8 stagger-fade-in">
					<header class="space-y-4 border-b border-iris/15 pb-7">
						<p class="eyebrow text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.28em]">Contact</p>
						<h1>Contact Zen Typer</h1>
						<p class="!text-lg !leading-8">
							Use the links below to reach Jonathan R. Reed about Zen Typer, report a problem, or share feedback about typing practice, accessibility, or privacy.
						</p>
					</header>

					<section class="space-y-4">
						<h2>Feedback and support</h2>
						<p>
							The best feedback is specific. If a quote looks broken, a typing state is confusing, a control is hard to reach with a keyboard, or a screen reader label does not match what is on screen, include the page, browser, device, and what happened. Accessibility reports are the most useful kind. The whole app is supposed to work without a mouse, so anything that breaks that is worth sending.
						</p>
						<p>
							You can reach Jonathan through the main website at <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">jonathanrreed.com</a> or through Bluesky at <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/thereedy.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@thereedy.bsky.social</a>. For project context and related work, visit <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com/projects/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jonathan R. Reed projects</a>.
						</p>
					</section>

					<section class="space-y-4">
						<h2>What to include</h2>
						<p>
							For bug reports, include whether you were using Quote Mode or Zen Mode, whether reduced motion was enabled, and whether the issue affected typing input, stats, drafts, settings, navigation, or display. For content suggestions, include the quote, author, or topic you think would improve the typing practice library.
						</p>
						<p>
							For accessibility reports, describe the control name, keyboard step, screen size, or assistive technology behavior that made the session harder to use. For privacy questions, note whether the concern involves local drafts, archived sessions, browser storage, external links, or hosting logs.
						</p>
						<p>
							Zen Typer is a small project, so a clear bug report is worth more here than a big feature request. The typing surface stays as it is; the fixes go to whatever is blocking practice, navigation, or reading.
						</p>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
